      "title": "Remotely debugging Firefox instances",
      "summary": "Previously I talked about remotely debugging Chrome , and we also covered the latest Microsoft Edge browser along the way. These features allow an adversary to gain access to authentication tokens and cookies. See MITRE ATT&CK Technique T1539: Steal Web Session Cookie as well for this. What about Firefox? For a while I was wondering if (my favorite) browser Firefox has such debugging features as well, and how one could detect malware trying to exploit it.",
